# places.py: the four wilds-north places, each with every row of its inventory.
# A row: id, kind, what (plain words), box (x0, y0, x1, y1 in the painting), shared ('here' = a shared id made in this
# place, a text = a shared id only listed here and made elsewhere, missing = not shared), optional src (another painting),
# optional refbox (the reference crop, if not the box), optional angle (turn the crop so a slanting thing runs level),
# stand (the patch for the stand-in: box, squash, angle) for ground and material rows made here, and prompt
# (title, subject, use, shape) for rows that get a ChatGPT prompt.
